<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!-- shifting.xml
Shifting is a method to improve the quality of the particle distribution 
and reduce numerical instabilities through the introduction of a small 
corrective displacement in the particle motion equation.

This corrective displacement is computed from local measures of disorder,
typically based on kernel gradients, and applied on top of the physical velocity field.

The shifting vector is evaluated using a the SPH approximation given in

Sun, P. N., et al. "A consistent approach to particle shifting in the δ-Plus-SPH model." 
Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering 348 (2019): 912-934.

There is a correction for particles close to BI boundaries. 

It is possible to add alternative formulations, just define the new one similar to:
"__SUN_SHIFTING__"

Remember that after including this preset, a new control parameter for each particle set 
should be imposed, the shifting factor (typically Uref = Ma cs), which scales the intensity
of the corrective displacement.

Optionally you can tune the effect of the anti-clumping term using the following definition:

- __AC_FACTOR__: Anticlumping term factor (R) for shifting (0.f by default)

To include it, just add this definition before loading the module:
    <Definitions>
        <Define name="__AC_FACTOR__" value="0.2" evaluate="false"/>
    </Definitions>
-->

<sphInput>
    <Variables>
        <Variable name="du_shift" type="vec*" length="N" />
	<Variable name="Uref" type="float" value="0.0" />
	<Variable name="gradC" type="vec*" length="N" />
    </Variables>

    <Definitions>
        <Define name="__SUN_SHIFTING__" value="1" evaluate="false"/>
        <Define name="__SHIFTING_FORMULATION__" value="__SUN_SHIFTING__" evaluate="false"/>
    </Definitions>

    <Tools>
	<Tool action="insert" after="Sort" type="set" name="cfd Reinit du_shift" in="du_shift" value="VEC_ZERO"/>
	<Tool action="insert" after="Sort" type="set" name="cfd Reinit gradC" in="gradC" value="VEC_ZERO"/>
        <Tool name="du gradC fluid" before="Interactions" type="kernel" action="insert" entry_point="drfluid" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting.cl"/>
        <Tool action="insert" before="Rates" type="kernel" name="cfd du" entry_point="du" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting.cl"/>
        <Tool action="insert" after="Corrector" type="kernel" name="cfd shifting" entry_point="correct" path="../../../Scripts/cfd/shifting/shifting.cl"/>
        </Tools>
</sphInput>
